# Gated paths: the files whose changes need the maintainer's judgement (docs/prd/32-code-review.md §3,
# D-022, D-056). This file does two jobs. GitHub requests a review from the owners when a pull request
# touches a listed path (except from the author of record, which is why the gate is a required status).
# .github/workflows/gate.yml reads this file from the base branch on every pull-request and review event
# and writes the required status `gate/maintainer`: a pull request that touches none of these paths
# passes; one that does passes only once a gate authority approved the current head (PR-REV-010). The
# `/.github/` line covers both gate.yml and gate-relay.yml. The list is mirrored
# by the `gate` entry of .github/labeler.yml, which routes gated pull requests to Greptile and to the
# maintainer; keep both in step with the PRD table.
#
# Owners: the maintainer. There are no teams on a personal account (D-057). When the backup admin is
# named (docs/prd/38-maintenance-and-support.md §8, bootstrap task 1), append their `@login` to every
# line below in the same pull request that sets the `BACKUP_ADMIN` Actions variable: gate.yml accepts
# their approval only while the `HANDOFF_ACTIVE` variable is `true`, never on this file alone.
#
# Syntax kept to the subset gate.yml matches: one pattern per line followed by owners, patterns
# anchored at the repository root with a leading `/`, a trailing `/` for a directory and its contents,
# `*` within one path segment. No negation, character classes or escapes.

# The source of truth: ID stability, event semantics and provenance define the product's trust claims.
